<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27397" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyrnēsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyrnessus</span></b> ), i, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυρνησός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Troas, the birthplace of
				Briseis</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30, 32, § 122</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyrnessi domus alta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 12, 547</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyrnēsĭus</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyrnessius</span></b> ),
				a, um, <i>adj., Lyrnesian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moenia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 108</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">13, 176</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 3,
			45</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyrnēsis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyr-nessis</span></b> ),
				ĭdis, f.
			adj. (only used as <i>subst.</i>), <i>the Lyrnesian</i> (sc. <i>maid</i> or
				<i>woman</i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abductā Lyrnesside tristis Achilles,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Briseis</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 4, 1, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">audierat, Lyrnessi, tuos, abducta, dolores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					A. 2, 403</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
